      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e     @Override\n\u003e     public List\u003cAccountGroup.UUID\u003e next() {\n\u003e       List\u003cAccountGroup.UUID\u003e batch \u003d new ArrayList\u003c\u003e(batchSize);\n\u003e       int count \u003d 0;\n\u003e       while (source.hasNext() \u0026\u0026 count++ \u003c batchSize) {\n\u003e         batch.add(source.next());\n\u003e       }\n\u003e       return batch;\n\u003e     }\n\u003e   }\n\u003e ```\n\u003e WDYT?\n\nI believe this also suffers from the same problem: we are creating a new array and copying the elements over. For reducing the memory consumption we should allocate a single array of batchSize and reuse it.\n\nI am wondering however if that could be simplified by just changing the input parameter from a `Set\u003c\u003e` to a `List\u003c\u003e`?",
